diagnosis_text:
- Affected component: OSPF adjacency to the WAN edge. CSW1’s OSPF process and all internal core adjacencies are healthy; the failure is the OSPF peering from CSW1 toward the WAN router (R1).
- Mechanism: With the CSW1–R1 OSPF neighbor down, no default route is injected into the IGP. Internal routes (between Offices A and B) remain via CSW1/CSW2 to the distribution switches, so inter-office pings still work. Internet-bound traffic fails due to the missing 0.0.0.0/0.
